# Normalise line endings so a Windows checkout behaves like a Linux one.
#
# Without this, Git's core.autocrlf on Windows rewrites every file to CRLF on
# checkout. Go source must stay LF: gofmt treats CRLF files as unformatted, so
# `gofmt -l .` fails on Windows CI even though the repository is clean.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.exe binary

# Scripts that must keep LF even if someone edits them on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
